picker.js and database.js here are copied from the published ESM of that version
(npm: emoji-picker-element@1.29.1) and modified for @docmd/plugin-threads.
Each modified file says so in a comment under its header.

Changes:
1. The custom element is registered as "threads-emoji-picker" instead of
   "emoji-picker" (still guarded: nothing happens if the tag is already defined),
   so a site that also uses emoji-picker has no clash.
2. The default data source (a jsDelivr CDN URL) is removed from picker.js and
   database.js. A missing dataSource is an error (Database throws); the emoji
   data is always served with the site.
3. The prefers-color-scheme: dark block is removed from the stylesheet. Colours
   come from the CSS custom properties that the host page sets on the element.
4. The UI strings are not changed in the file: the host sets the "i18n" property
   from the plugin's own translations. The upstream i18n files are not included.

Nothing else differs from the upstream files, apart from the two comment headers.
